=head1 DESCRIPTION

The parameters that define or describe the historical data that your
auto-adjusting budget is based on.

=head1 ATTRIBUTES


=head2 B<REQUIRED> BudgetAdjustmentPeriod => Int

The number of budget periods included in the moving-average calculation
that determines your auto-adjusted budget amount. The maximum value
depends on the C<TimeUnit> granularity of the budget:

=over

=item *

For the C<DAILY> granularity, the maximum value is C<60>.

=item *

For the C<MONTHLY> granularity, the maximum value is C<12>.

=item *

For the C<QUARTERLY> granularity, the maximum value is C<4>.

=item *

For the C<ANNUALLY> granularity, the maximum value is C<1>.

=back



=head2 LookBackAvailablePeriods => Int

The integer that describes how many budget periods in your
C<BudgetAdjustmentPeriod> are included in the calculation of your
current C<BudgetLimit>. If the first budget period in your
C<BudgetAdjustmentPeriod> has no cost data, then that budget period
isnE<rsquo>t included in the average that determines your budget limit.

For example, if you set C<BudgetAdjustmentPeriod> as C<4> quarters, but
your account had no cost data in the first quarter, then only the last
three quarters are included in the calculation. In this scenario,
C<LookBackAvailablePeriods> returns C<3>.

You canE<rsquo>t set your own C<LookBackAvailablePeriods>. The value is
automatically calculated from the C<BudgetAdjustmentPeriod> and your
historical cost data.



